This page contains a list of lujvo that I (Robin Powell) created programmatically.  All the lujvo listed here (that say "not found in database", at least) are those that are mentioned in the gismu or cmavo lists but don't have active definitions in jbovlaste.

If you make one of these words, it is polite to remove it here, but don't worry about it *too* much.

-Robin

Also, some of these lujvo are not actually in the canonical (lowest-scoring) form. Please check their canonicity with jvocuhadju or some such.

-Arnt Richard

__{jvsv balzgibe'e}__


 bende bed     be'e crew                 ' band '
                    x1 is a crew/team/gang/squad/band of persons x2
                    directed/led by x3 organized for purpose x4

                    (x1 is a mass; x2 is a set completely specified);
                    ~np~[also orchestra (= zgibe'e, __balzgibe'e__), outfit; x3
                    conductor; business, not necessarily incorporated (=
                    cajbe'e, venbe'e)]~/np~; (cf. gunma, girzu, dansu, jatna,
                    jitro, kagni, kamni, minde, ralju, cecmu, gidva)

__{jvsv basysakta}__


 sakta sat          sugar                ' sucrose '
                    x1 is made of/contains/is a quantity of sugar ~np~[sweet
                    edible]~/np~ from source x2 of composition x3

                    ~np~[also sucrose, fructose, glucose, galactose, lactose,
                    etc.; saccharine/aspartame/sugar substitute (__basysakta__
                    or sakybasti, ticysakta); x3: composition including
                    x3, which need not be complete specification]~/np~;
                    (cf. silna, titla)

__{jvsv batygre}__


 batci bat          bite
                    x1 bites/pinches x2 on/at specific locus x3 with x4

                    ~np~[bite through (= ka'arbatci, __batygre__); pinch (=
                    cinzybatci)]~/np~; (cf. denci, jgalu, guska, citka)

__{jvsv bavla'ima'i}__


 masti         ma'i month
                    x1 is x2 months in duration (default is 1 month)
                    by month standard x3

                    ~np~[this month (= cabma'i); next month (= __bavla'ima'i__);
                    last month (= prula'ima'i)]~/np~; (cf. detri, djedi,
                    jeftu, nanca)

__{jvsv bavlamcerni}__


 cerni cer          morning
                    x1 is a morning ~np~[dawn until after typical
                    start-of-work for locale]~/np~ of day x2 at location x3

                    ~np~[this morning (= cabdeicerni); tomorrow morning
                    (= __bavlamcerni__); yesterday morning (= prulamcerni,
                    prulamdeicerni)]~/np~(cf. vanci, murse, tcika)

__{jvsv bavlamcte}__


 nicte     cte      night
                    x1 is a nighttime of day x2 at location x3;
                    (adjective:) x1 is at night/nocturnal

                    ~np~[tonight (= cabycte); tomorrow night (= __bavlamcte__,
                    even when tonight is still in the future); last night
                    (= prulamcte)]~/np~; (cf. donri, djedi, tcika)

__{jvsv bavlamna'a}__


 nanca         na'a year
                    x1 is x2 years in duration (default is 1 year)
                    by standard x3; (adjective:) x1 is annual

                    ~np~[this year (= cabna'a); next year (= __bavlamna'a__); last
                    year (= prulamna'a)]~/np~; (cf. detri, djedi, jeftu, masti)

__{jvsv be'ejda}__


 lijda     jda      religion
                    x1 is a religion of believers including x2 sharing
                    common beliefs/practices/tenets including x3

                    ~np~[also mythos, creed, traditional beliefs,
                    x2 people(s), adherents; (adjective:) x1, x2,
                    x3 are religious/ecclesiastic in nature; x2 is a
                    believer in/of x1, an adherent/follower of x1 (=
                    seljda for reordered places); x2 is a practitioner
                    of x3 (= selterjda for reordered places); x3 is a
                    tenet/belief/ritual/creed of x1/x2 (= terjda for
                    reordered places); priest/clerical (= jdaca'i,
                    jdaka'i, jdaja'a); organized church/religion
                    (= __be'ejda__); congregation (= jdabe'e, jdagri)]~/np~;
                    (cf. budjo, censa, cevni, crida, dadjo, jegvo,
                    krici, latna, malsi, marde, muslo, pruxi, ranmi,
                    ritli, xriso, zekri)

__{jvsv befctirango}__


 betfu bef     be'u abdomen              ' belly '
                    x1 is a/the abdomen/belly/lower trunk ~np~[body-part]~/np~
                    of x2; ~np~[metaphor: midsection]~/np~

                    ~np~[also stomach (= djaruntyrango), digestive tract
                    (= __befctirango__, befctirangyci'e)]~/np~; (cf. cutne,
                    livga, canti)

__{jvsv befctirangyci'e}__


 betfu bef     be'u abdomen              ' belly '
                    x1 is a/the abdomen/belly/lower trunk ~np~[body-part]~/np~
                    of x2; ~np~[metaphor: midsection]~/np~

                    ~np~[also stomach (= djaruntyrango), digestive tract
                    (= befctirango, __befctirangyci'e__)]~/np~; (cf. cutne,
                    livga, canti)

__{jvsv bi'agla}__


 glare     gla      hot                  ' warm '
                    x1 is hot/~np~[warm]~/np~ by standard x2

                    ~np~[warm (= mligla), feverish (= __bi'agla__)]~/np~; (cf. lenku)

__{jvsv bilpre}__


 bilni bil          military
                    x1 is military/regimented/is strongly
                    organized/prepared by system x2 for purpose x3

                    ~np~[also paramilitary; soldier in its broadest sense -
                    not limited to those trained/organized as part of
                    an army to defend a state (= __bilpre__)]~/np~; (cf. jenmi
                    for a military force, sonci, ganzu, pulji)

__{jvsv bilpulji}__


 pulji              police
                    x1 is a police officer/~np~[enforcer/vigilante]~/np~ enforcing
                    law(s)/rule(s)/order x2

                    ~np~[police officer, as an agent of authority (=
                    ca'irpulji, ka'irpulji), as part of a police force (=
                    puljysoi, as part of puljyselsoi); military police
                    (= jempulji, __bilpulji__)]~/np~; (cf. catni, sonci, bilni,
                    flalu, bandu, jemna, zekri, krati)

__{jvsv binryvelve'u}__


 binra              insure
                    x1 insures/indemnifies x2 (person) against peril x3
                    (event) providing benefit(s) x4 (event)

                    ~np~[also x3 loss; sell/purchase insurance (= binryve'u),
                    premium (= binrydi'a, or __binryvelve'u__)]~/np~; (cf. bandu,
                    cirko, betri, basti, bilma)

__{jvsv birgutci}__


 gutci guc          cubit                ' foot '
                    x1 is x2 (default 1) short local distance unit(s)
                    ~np~[non-metric]~/np~, standard x3, x4 subunits

                    ~np~[foot (= jmagutci); yard (= cibjmagutci), pace (=
                    tapygutci), inch (= degygutci), cubit (= __birgutci__)]~/np~;
                    (additional subunit places may be added as x5, x6,
                    ...); (cf. mitre, clani, ganra, condi, rotsu, rupnu,
                    fepni, dekpu, minli, merli, bunda, kramu)

__{jvsv blikubli}__


 bliku     bli      block
                    x1 is a block ~np~[3-dimensional shape/form]~/np~ of material
                    x2, surfaces/sides x3

                    ~np~[x3 sides/surfaces should include number, size, and
                    shape; also polyhedron (= pitybli having flat/planar
                    sides/surfaces)]~/np~, regular polyhedron (= kubybli,
                    __blikubli__), brick (= kitybli); (cf. tapla, kubli,
                    tanbo, canlu, kojna, sefta, bolci, kurfa, tarmi)

__{jvsv blixra}__


 pixra pir xra      picture
                    x1 is a picture/illustration representing/showing x2,
                    made by artist x3 in medium x4

                    ~np~[also (adjective:) x1 is pictorial/illustrative;
                    drawing (= xraselci'a), x1 draws x2 (=
                    xraci'a/xraci'a), image (= xratai), photo (=
                    kacmyxra), take a photo (= kacmyterxra, kacmyxragau,
                    kacmyxrazu'e); sculpture, relief (= __blixra__)]~/np~;
                    (cf. ciska, cinta, prina, mupli, barna, skina)

__{jvsv bonka'u}__


 kantu         ka'u quantum
                    x1 is a quantum/ray/elementary particle/smallest
                    measurable increment of property/activity x2

                    ~np~[quantum ray (= __bonka'u__)]~/np~; (cf. selci for masses
                    and most objects; ratni, gradu, gusni, nejni, linji)

__{jvsv ca'ermuvgau}__


 catke         ca'e shove
                    x1 ~np~[agent]~/np~ shoves/pushes x2 at locus x3

                    ~np~[move by pushing/shoving (= __ca'ermuvgau__)]~/np~; (cf. danre
                    for non-agentive force, lacpu)

__{jvsv ca'irpulji}__


 pulji              police
                    x1 is a police officer/~np~[enforcer/vigilante]~/np~ enforcing
                    law(s)/rule(s)/order x2

                    ~np~[police officer, as an agent of authority (=
                    __ca'irpulji__, ka'irpulji), as part of a police force (=
