__{jvsv cinzybatci}__


 batci bat          bite
                    x1 bites/pinches x2 on/at specific locus x3 with x4

                    ~np~[bite through (= ka'arbatci, batygre); pinch (=
                    __cinzybatci__)]~/np~; (cf. denci, jgalu, guska, citka)

__{jvsv cirsau}__


 slabu         sau  familiar
                    x1 is old/familiar/well-known to observer x2 in
                    feature x3 (ka) by standard x4

                    ~np~[This can cover both meanings of old.  Old in years,
                    i.e. age, can be conveyed through x2 = the world,
                    life, existence (= loi nu zasti); in usage this has
                    been a common default for ellipsis.  However slabu is
                    not the opposite of ' young ' (= nalci'o, tolci'o),
                    but the opposite of 'new' (= tolni'o); also ancient
                    (= tcesau), age (= nilsau); x2 is used to x1 (=
                    selsau for reordered places); historic/historical (=
                    __cirsau__, cirselcedra; also vaipru)]~/np~; (cf. clani, citno,
                    cnino, se djuno; not the opposite of citno, djuno)

__{jvsv cirselcedra}__


 slabu         sau  familiar
                    x1 is old/familiar/well-known to observer x2 in
                    feature x3 (ka) by standard x4

                    ~np~[This can cover both meanings of old.  Old in years,
                    i.e. age, can be conveyed through x2 = the world,
                    life, existence (= loi nu zasti); in usage this has
                    been a common default for ellipsis.  However slabu is
                    not the opposite of ' young ' (= nalci'o, tolci'o),
                    but the opposite of 'new' (= tolni'o); also ancient
                    (= tcesau), age (= nilsau); x2 is used to x1 (=
                    selsau for reordered places); historic/historical (=
                    cirsau, __cirselcedra__; also vaipru)]~/np~; (cf. clani, citno,
                    cnino, se djuno; not the opposite of citno, djuno)

