__{jvsv cismyfra}__


 cisma              smile
                    x1 smiles/grins (facial expression)

                    ~np~[smile/grin at something (= __cismyfra__)]~/np~; (cf. xajmi,
                    cmila, frumu)

__{jvsv citsydei}__


 citsi              season
                    x1 is a season/is seasonal ~np~[cyclical interval]~/np~,
                    defined by interval/property x2, of year(s) x3

                    ~np~[also anniversary (= __citsydei__, na'ar__citsydei__),
                    jubilee (= mumnoncitsi); the period of time may be
                    short or long as indicated by x2, and may occur every
                    year or every nth year as indicated by x3 (default
                    every year); (x2 and/or x3 may need metaphorical
                    restriction: djecitsi, pavdeicitsi; also equinox,
                    solstice, time of year]~/np~; (cf. cedra, crisa, critu,
                    dunra, ranji, temci, vensa, jbena)

__{jvsv citsyti'a}__


 tcima tim     ti'a weather              ' climate '
                    x1 is weather at place/region x2; (adjective:)
                    x1 is meteorological

                    ~np~[climate (= __citsyti'a__, timymo'a)]~/np~; (cf. brife, bumru,
                    carvi, dilnu, bratu)

__{jvsv citxarju}__


 xarju xaj          pig                  ' hog '
                    x1 is a pig/hog/swine/~np~[boar]~/np~ ~np~[pork/ham/bacon-producer]~/np~
                    of species/breed x2

                    ~np~[sow (= fetxarju), boar (= nakyxarju), pork (=
                    xajre'u), piglet (= __citxarju__)]~/np~; (cf. mabru, cange)

__{jvsv claboi}__


 sovda sov     so'a egg                  ' ovum '
                    x1 is an egg/ovum/sperm/pollen/gamete of/from organism
                    ~np~[mother/father]~/np~ x2

                    ~np~[(poorly metaphorical only due to gender- and species-
                    being unspecified): ovoid, oblate (= pevyso'aseltai,
                    but better: __claboi__); egg, specifically female (=
                    fetso'a), of a bird (= cpifetso'a, cpiso'a), of a
                    chicken (= jipcyfetso'a, jipcyso'a]~/np~ (but note that
                    Lojban does not require specificity, just as English
                    doesn't for either milk or eggs; "sovda" is fine for
                    most contexts); ~np~[if fertilized, then tsiju or tarbi]~/np~;
                    (cf. ganti, gutra, mamta, patfu, rorci, tsiju, lanbi,
                    tarbi; also djine, konju for shape, tarbi)

