__{jvsv guntrusi'o}__


 turni     tru      govern
                    x1 governs/rules/is ruler/governor/sovereign/reigns
                    over people/territory/domain/subjects x2

                    ~np~[x2 need not be complete specification of set of
                    governed; reign/rule (= noltru); king/queen/sovereign
                    (= nolraitru); pure democracy (= roltrusi'o),
                    representative democracy (= rolka'itrusi'o), viceroy
                    (= ka'itru), pure communism (= __guntrusi'o__), board of
                    directors/trustees, steering committee (= trukamni);
                    government (= trugunma, trugri (emphasizing the
                    components), truci'e (emphasizing the organization))]~/np~;
                    (cf. catni, minde, tutra, jecta, gugde, ponse, jitro)

__{jvsv gusmo'a}__


 morna mon     mo'a pattern              ' form '
                    x1 is/reflects/represents a pattern of forms/events
                    x2 arranged according to structure x3

                    ~np~[x3 is a [((jbovlaste import: model]~/np~ for x1 (= termontai, or the more
                    abstract = termonsi'o); image (= __gusmo'a__, nenmo'a,
                    dairmo'a, selylenmo'a, selmirmo'a, velmirmo'a, but
                    also all of these -tai instead of -mo'a for the
                    ideal) lang en)); (cf. ciste, ganzu, marji, slilu, stura,
                    tarmi, boxna, cimde, gidva, jimpe, rilti)

__{jvsv jabdesku}__


 janbe jab          bell
                    x1 is a bell/chime/~np~[tuning fork]~/np~ ~np~[tuned percussion
                    instrument]~/np~ producing sound/note x2

                    ~np~[also: x1 rings/tolls (i.e. if it rings, then it
                    is a bell); resonates (one sense, = __jabdesku__)]~/np~;
                    (cf. zgike, tonga, desku, slilu)

__{jvsv jacfanxi'u}__


 falnu fan          sail
                    x1 is a sail for gathering propelling material x2
                    on vehicle/motor x3

                    ~np~[waterwheel (= __jacfanxi'u__)]~/np~; (cf. bloti)

__{jvsv jaupli}__


 djacu jac     jau  water                'aqua-'
                    x1 is made of/contains/is a quantity/expanse of water;
                    (adjective:) x1 is aqueous/~np~[aquatic]~/np~

                    ~np~[aquatic (= __jaupli__)]~/np~; (cf. lalxu, rirxe, xamsi,
                    limna, litki, lumci, bumru, jinto)

__{jvsv jdabe'e}__


 lijda     jda      religion
                    x1 is a religion of believers including x2 sharing
                    common beliefs/practices/tenets including x3

                    ~np~[also mythos, creed, traditional beliefs,
                    x2 people(s), adherents; (adjective:) x1, x2,
                    x3 are religious/ecclesiastic in nature; x2 is a
                    believer in/of x1, an adherent/follower of x1 (=
                    seljda for reordered places); x2 is a practitioner
                    of x3 (= selterjda for reordered places); x3 is a
                    tenet/belief/ritual/creed of x1/x2 (= terjda for
                    reordered places); priest/clerical (= jdaca'i,
                    jdaka'i, jdaja'a); organized church/religion
                    (= be'ejda); congregation (= __jdabe'e__, jdagri)]~/np~;
                    (cf. budjo, censa, cevni, crida, dadjo, jegvo,
                    krici, latna, malsi, marde, muslo, pruxi, ranmi,
                    ritli, xriso, zekri)

